# CEG: bible-project — Hebrew database + translation website
# Repo: kitcosby/bible-project (public; originally cosbykit-afk/bible-project)
# Grounded in website/app_v2.py routes and schema_v2.sql (v2 normalized corpus).
# Public-domain sources only.
#
# v2 normalization (2026-09-28, commits 937ccc7 + 8e71728):
# - schema_v2.sql: base tables normalized (words, verses, root_entry/form/vowel,
#   morph_patterns/segments, strongs_sources, lexicon_* child tables, glosses,
#   kjv_words, ylt_verses/renderings). bible_v2.db opened READ-ONLY by app_v2.
# - Derived-data stage (built after migrate; never alters base tables):
#   build_alignment.py -> word_alignment (836,290 rows; Hebrew/KJV/YLT links);
#   build_variants.py -> word_variants (528,565 rows; v1-medial vs academic-final);
#   apply_morph_corrections.py -> morph_variants (28 rows, 12 words; established
#   corrections re-point words.morph_pattern_id, probable/secondary staged only).
# - app_v2.py: faithful port of app.py to the v2 corpus. Routes, forms, redirects,
#   export format, choice-file format unchanged. Queries read normalized tables;
#   child-table row order preserves v1 blob order so drop-downs render identically.
# - Word detail (v2) additionally shows: Strong's source (strongs_sources),
#   YLT verse contexts (lexicon_ylt_context, resolved refs), Found verses
#   (lexicon_found_verse, resolved refs). Affixes row still from *_disp (U-7).
# - v2 also fixes the /bible "Books" link bug (mount-prefix aware via SCRIPT_NAME).
# - Derived tables (word_alignment, morph_variants) are NOT yet surfaced in the
#   website UI; they are build-pipeline outputs, not modeled here.
# - word_variants IS now surfaced: /variants route (2026-09-30) — Hebrew word
#   drop-down + search box, variant readings table per word (528,565 rows,
#   all variant_kind='spelling' so far; witness/variant_type columns ready).
# - Interlinear view (2026-09-30, Kit-approved wireframe): /interlinear/<b>/<c>/<v>
#   — Hebrew words in Hebrew order (RTL) each with variant + translation
#   drop-downs; English sentence below in KJV word order from word_alignment /
#   kjv_words, KJV words with no Hebrew alignment italicized (KJV print
#   convention); dynamic Book/Chapter/Verse drop-downs via /api/*; Prev/Next
#   verse links roll over chapter and book boundaries; word detail page gains
#   a Bibliomancy section listing every verse using the word form.
# - QA driver (drivers/bible.py) ported to app_v2.py + bible_v2.db 2026-09-28.
# - 2026-09-30 Kit adjudication on export formats: an unrecognized format is
#   NOT invalid (Kit: possibly highly archaic vowel structures) — the app
#   must never reject it. New expectation e18: the export flags the format
#   for further research and still renders the full translation with special
#   characters displayed. Old f5 ("rejects unsupported format") was a model
#   error, not a product bug.
# - Clean reading view (2026-09-30, Kit): /reading/<tid>/<b>/<c>/<v> is now
#   NOTHING but the English translation as exported — no interlinear, no
#   drop-downs, no Hebrew spans, no navigation chrome. Unknown verses 404.
# - User accounts (2026-09-30, Kit): user_accounts table (salted password
#   hashes, never cleartext); /signup, /login, /logout; translations created
#   while logged in record owner_id. Kit's translation-source integer is
#   recorded on lemma_default: 1=KJV, 2=Young's, 3=user-defined (source 3
#   links to other_option via other_option_id).
# - Variant de-dup (2026-09-30, Kit): the v1-medial vs academic-final rows
#   are NOT real manuscript variance — dirty data from the study tool, which
#   ignored special characters for end-of-word letterforms. Rows differing
#   ONLY by medial/final letterforms (fold_finals) are folded away and never
#   baked into the UI. Kit 2026-10-01: v1 data-artifact rows (basis marking
#   anomaly= or ARTIFACT) are excluded from variant display entirely — only
#   academic/textual manuscript variants count. No textual rows are loaded
#   yet, so the /variants drop-down is empty with an explanatory note until
#   real apparatus data arrives. Words with no real variance show "none"
#   instead of the drop-down (interlinear).
# - DB QA applications (2026-11-11, Kit-approved; issues #20/#21/#23):
#   verse-grid repair refiled 92 misfiled words to their true verses
#   (Esth 4:4, Ps 17:1, Isa 27:1, Jer 28:1, Lam 2:1 filled); 18 exact
#   Strong's fills applied (blank Strong's now 4,321 in both stores);
#   split_multi_strongs resolved as COMPOSITE values in words.strongs
#   (comma-joined in maqqef-chain order, components in strongs_components,
#   source oshb-split; 135 words) — new cause c19 / effect e41;
#   PARALLEL-CONFLATE distribution pass on ylt_renderings (357,574 rows;
#   shared YLT positions 11,448 -> 10,642); local corpus and production
#   PostgreSQL verified in full content-hash parity (words, YLT,
#   word_alignment, lexicon_ylt_rendering).
# - Hidden verse shells (2026-11-11, Kit ruled "leave the rows but hide
#   them"): the 7 verse rows emptied by the grid repair (Ps 17:17,
#   Isa 27:22, Jer 28:23, Lam 2:23, Josh 4:32, 2 Chr 36:32, Ruth 8:18)
#   are KEPT in the grid (each retains its Peshitta no_counterpart note)
#   and flagged verses.hidden = 1 in schema_v2.sql and both stores.
#   app_v2 honors the flag in the shared _WORDS_EXIST fragment, the HTML
#   book/chapter listings, and the read-view navigation helpers
#   (_chapter_bounds, _last_chapter) — new cause c18 / effects e40, f11.
#   Verified live in production 2026-11-11: /api/chapters/8 = [1,2,3,4],
#   /api/verse/19/17/17 = 404, /api/verses/19/17 = 1..15, read view for
#   Ruth 4 offers no chapter-8 navigation.
#
# ROOT SPLIT (2026-11-12, Kit's authoring lesson — see CEG_FORMAT.md):
# This file is the ROOT branch of the bible-project graph. The graph opens
# with a big one-and-only-one — the page — that splits: each branch
# generates on its own with only its own inputs, instead of one
# cross-product of all 20 inputs (46,006,272 combinations, un-generatable).
# Branches: bible-project.ceg (index/book/chapter + site-wide effects),
# bible-project-verse.ceg (verse/choice/reading/export),
# bible-project-word.ceg (word detail), bible-project-variants.ceg
# (variants), bible-project-interlinear.ceg (interlinear),
# bible-project-account.ceg (signup/login/translations).
# Requirement ids keep their REQ-BB numbers in whichever branch carries
# them; split requirements are noted where they live.

[PAGE]
Bible website root pages (v2): index, book, chapter. Database:
bible_v2.db (v2 normalized). Branch files cover the remaining pages:
verse, choice, translations, reading, export, word detail, variants,
interlinear, signup, login.

[INPUTS]
c0 = page : index | book | chapter
c1 = ref_valid : no | yes
c18 = verse_hidden : no | yes

[CONSTRAINTS]
# Root branch of the page one-and-only-one: this branch carries only the
# inputs its own pages use. No success input here is page-foreign, so no
# further constraint is needed — the split itself is the constraint.

[SUCCESS]
e1 = index lists the books
e1 <= c0=index
e2 = book page lists its chapters
e2 <= c0=book AND c1=yes
e3 = chapter page lists its verses
e3 <= c0=chapter AND c1=yes
e22 = index page links to the variants page
e22 <= c0=index
e36 = every standard page (index, book, chapter, verse, word, variants, translations, interlinear, signup, login) references the papyrus tile background
e36 <= c0=index
e40 = listings and read navigation omit hidden verses: chapter lists contain no chapter whose verses are all hidden (Ruth offers chapters 1-4 only), verse lists exclude hidden verses, and Prev/Next navigation never lands on a hidden verse
e40 <= c18=yes

[FAIL]
f1 = book page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f1 <= c0=book AND c1=no
f2 = chapter page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f2 <= c0=chapter AND c1=no

[REQUIREMENTS]
REQ-BB-001 : index lists the books -> e1
REQ-BB-002 : book and chapter pages list chapters and verses for valid references -> e2, e3
REQ-BB-008 : invalid references show not-found on book, chapter, verse, and reading pages (verse and reading halves in bible-project-verse.ceg) -> f1, f2
REQ-BB-011 : variants page offers the Hebrew word drop-down with search and shows variant readings; index links to it (page halves in bible-project-variants.ceg) -> e22
REQ-BB-016 : site-wide papyrus visual theme: every standard page references the papyrus tile background -> e36
REQ-BB-018 : verses flagged hidden are retained in the data but never render: absent from chapter/verse listings and read navigation (not-found halves in bible-project-verse.ceg and bible-project-interlinear.ceg) -> e40
